Tom,

Richard's response is probably directed at me, too.  I tend to use the "raw" values in the "@opt" section of the occu results rather than using the helper functions linearComb, backTransform, and confint.  So to get the equivalent of what I sent with those functions (and the confidence intervals) here are some examples using your model results.

Assuming you want the estimates and confidence intervals for the detection probabilities for a single visit with 5 trap nights and both the road camera active and inactive, here are some commands to do so:

# Estimate of detection probability for road camera active with 5 trap nights
backTransform(linearComb(results['det'], c(1, 1, 5)))
#Backtransformed linear combination(s) of Detection estimate(s)
#
# Estimate     SE LinComb (Intercept) road effort
#    0.268 0.0272   -1.01           1    1      5
#
#Transformation: logistic

# Estimate of detection probability for road camera inactive with 5 trap nights
backTransform(linearComb(results['det'], c(1, 0, 5)))
#Backtransformed linear combination(s) of Detection estimate(s)
#
# Estimate     SE LinComb (Intercept) road effort
#    0.109 0.0147    -2.1           1    0      5
#
#Transformation: logistic

# Confidence interval for detection probability for road camera active with 5 trap nights confint(backTransform(linearComb(results['det'], c(1, 1, 5))))
#     0.025     0.975
# 0.2179388 0.3243997

# Confidence interval for detection probability for road camera inactive with 5 trap nights
confint(backTransform(linearComb(results['det'], c(1, 0, 5))))
#      0.025     0.975
# 0.08380726 0.1417416

There are a variety of ways to grab the output to produce a graphic.

Jim

